Chapter: FieldRangeProven

 Regression guard for the checker-side lint's field-access arm.

 A bounded field read used to prove as the full i64 range, because
 aexpr-proven-range had no arm for it -- the emit prover carried one
 all along. So b.val / 16 over 0..255, which is exactly 0..15, was
 rejected at a Nibble store the emitter could have proven safe.

 The .diag pins CDX2053 rather than mere compilation: the arm's whole
 point is that the range is PROVEN, so a regression that loses it
 would still compile here by falling back to a runtime check, and
 only the absent proof would show it.

Section: Definitions

  Byte = record {
   val : Integer between 0 and 255
  }

  Nibble = record {
   n : Integer between 0 and 15
  }

  high-nibble : Byte -> Integer
  high-nibble (b) = (Nibble { n = b.val / 16 }).n

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   print-line-uni (integer-to-text (high-nibble (Byte { val = 200 })))
  end
